  "cover_text": "I was watching TV with Devin the other day and saw some of this theory on random transmission: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Return_metastability\n\nI started wondering about this quite recently, and also about this simplification: https://math.stackexchange.com/questions/2806840/return-metastability-calling-re-technically-null-by-definition\n\nIf I have a self-organizing bias around some set of configurations then I accept that the system will not undergo metapixne stability, meaning that a self-organizing bias will do things like clustering around this set of configurations, and reduce",
